diff --git a/readme-dev.md b/readme-dev.md
index 58dd0e8..c1df926 100644
--- a/readme-dev.md
+++ b/readme-dev.md
@@ -1,11 +1,22 @@
 This package uses the bundled `@openai/codex` dependency by default.
 Set `CODEX_PATH` to run a different Codex binary; versions other than the one specified in `package.json` may not be compatible.
 
+This Zed Test build connects through `codex app-server proxy` to the existing shared daemon. It never starts or stops an app-server daemon. Closing a session or losing the editor connection detaches the client without sending `turn/interrupt`, including turns started by Zed and in-flight `turn/start` requests. Explicit `session/cancel` or prompt-request cancellation on a live connection still interrupts the turn. The daemon must already be running, and the Codex binary must support `app-server proxy`.
+
+### History pagination
+
+Zed Test advertises `_meta["zed.dev/historyPagination"]: {"version": 1}` in its client capabilities. With this capability, `session/load` replays only the last 100 native history items and returns `_meta["zed.dev/historyPagination"].nextCursor`. Older clients continue to receive the full replay.
+
+To fetch earlier history, the client sends the ACP extension request `_zed/history/page` with `{sessionId, cursor}`. The response contains `{updates, nextCursor}` in chronological order. These updates are returned separately from live `session/update` notifications so the client can prepend them without moving existing content. Cursors belong to one session load and can be retried; `null` means the beginning of the history was reached.
+
+Paging only affects displayed history, never the model's context. Paginated Codex stores use bounded `thread/items/list` reads. Legacy stores require one full history read, retained in the adapter and delivered to Zed one page at a time. Reading an older page does not resume the thread or create a turn.
+
 ### Runtime environment
 
 - `CODEX_API_KEY` - API key used when the API-key auth method is selected. Takes precedence over `OPENAI_API_KEY`.
 - `OPENAI_API_KEY` - fallback API key used when the API-key auth method is selected.
 - `CODEX_PATH` - run a specific Codex executable instead of the bundled package dependency.
+- `CODEX_APP_SERVER_SOCKET` - optional Unix socket path for the shared daemon; defaults to the Codex control socket.
 - `CODEX_CONFIG` - JSON object merged into the Codex session config.
 - `MODEL_PROVIDER` - model provider to pass to Codex for new sessions.
 - `DEFAULT_AUTH_REQUEST` - ACP auth request JSON used when Codex requires authentication.
@@ -102,4 +113,3 @@ the adapter does not rely on notices being displayed.
 Command replies, review results, and terminal/retrying errors retain their existing response or
 failure channels. Clients advertising session compaction support continue to receive the dedicated
 compaction lifecycle instead of the legacy completion advisory.
